    <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Kayden</span> sniffles and buries his face in his arms, <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“But I want you to stay today.”</span> Seems <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Kayden</span> was feeling a bit clingy today, as usual for kids his age, but you still feel sad looking at his little face. <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Hakeem</span> sighs once more, <span style="Color: Yellow">his face a mix of guilt and helplessness as he stands back up.</span> <br>
    <br>
    <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“He’s been like this since this morning. Think he had a bad dream or something. I’d stay home if it wasn’t important.”</span> You nod, assuring <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Kayden</span> that the two of you will have a good time and his dad will be home before he knows it. <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Hakeem</span> gives you a thankful smile before returning to his son. <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“I know it’s hard, but I promise I’ll be back. And you’re going to have a great time tonight, just like you always do.”</span> He gives <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Kayden</span> a hug before waving goodbye and heading out to the car. <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Kayden</span> continues to sit there for a while before eventually getting up, <span style="Color: Yellow">still looking a bit upset.</span> <br>
